# Shell scripts must be checked out with LF, always.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which
# rewrites checked-out files to CRLF. That is harmless for YAML, C# and
# markdown, but it breaks shell scripts in two ways that are hard to
# diagnose:
#
#   - a CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally
#     named "/usr/bin/env bash\r", which fails as "bad interpreter", and
#   - deploy/glitchtip-minio/provision.sh is piped into the Linux `minio`
#     container, where CRLF also breaks its heredoc terminator.
#
# Both would only appear on a fresh clone, not for whoever wrote the file,
# which is the worst way to find out.
*.sh text eol=lf
